    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d287">

                <pb facs="0336" n="260" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg260"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 422.11G93/830</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Hartman to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Quito</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-01-11T16:00:00-05:14">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 11, 1916, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Referring to my cable of October 28, 10 a.m.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d287-f1"/> I am
                    informed by the president of the Guayaquil &amp; Quito Railway Company that
                    negotiations for private settlement of differences with Ecuadorean Government
                    have failed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hartman</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
